From 87d1bb7ec6bbb7231b6fd07da7f1655c53f7cfbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:23:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] xocl, common: put storage class and inline first
 (-Wold-style-declaration)

Mainline commit f5982cceb347 ("kbuild: turn on -Wextra by default",
v6.10) makes every external module build with -Wextra, which includes
-Wold-style-declaration. Declarations such as "static void inline f()"
and "const static T t[]" then warn; the three inline helpers in
include/xrt_cu.h alone produce 3 warnings in each of the ~70 objects
that include it (339 warnings per build on 6.11 .. 7.0).

Reorder the specifiers ("static inline void", "static const ...") in
include/xrt_cu.h, include/kds_ert_table.h, subdev/xmc.c,
subdev/firewall.c, subdev/clock_wiz.c and subdev/xgq_vmr.c.

Guard: none needed; this is the standard C spelling on every compiler
and kernel, the old one is only an obsolescent form of the same
declaration.

Equivalence: exact; specifier order has no meaning to the compiler.

Upstream: the xrt_cu.h and kds_ert_table.h hunks are those of XRT
commit d1fbc5cea ("Added 6.12 kernel support to the zocl"); XRT master
still has the other sites.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
